WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.648
At the end of the twelfth century, the Mongol steppe was filled with rival tribes, at war year after year.

00:00:06.998 --> 00:00:10.238
The herders on the steppe all longed for peace.

00:00:10.588 --> 00:00:16.060
Temujin grew up in hardship from childhood and resolved to unite the steppe.

00:00:16.410 --> 00:00:19.266
He grew up step by step through wind and snow.

00:00:19.616 --> 00:00:23.384
One after another, he defeated the powerful rivals of the steppe.

00:00:23.734 --> 00:00:26.590
His force grew stronger day by day.

00:00:26.940 --> 00:00:32.772
In the year 1206, the chiefs of the tribes raised Temujin up as Genghis Khan.

00:00:33.122 --> 00:00:36.674
Beneath the nine white yak-tail banners, everyone cheered together.

00:00:37.024 --> 00:00:41.104
Under his leadership, the Mongol tribes were formed into a powerful force.

00:00:41.454 --> 00:00:45.486
The horsemen rode shoulder to shoulder across the steppe.

00:00:45.836 --> 00:00:49.964
This year became a brand-new starting point in Mongol history.

00:00:50.314 --> 00:00:55.738
The golden morning sun rose slowly and lit up the vast steppe.

